"commit_sha":"9f2c5c0cec3542127fc29cd9d6e2355c554698b8","position":"1795279764169608001-c1943a27-b90e-4adb-9700-a0b0cf9b3dbd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"b41893893547555bf703e218254dd5189400f707970703dad6d31a59b120858b","event_uuid":"f86d8a45-a5f1-4ceb-8154-0f0ae4f325f3","position":{"commit_sha":"9313652cf81283ace5eddd2ab9b841ecbaed9fd1","position":"1795280539741230001-f86d8a45-a5f1-4ceb-8154-0f0ae4f325f3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"eb82d5b6a434ccb1e95336b93c8cc0c3535f5868fdaa415cccb4113bb6161eff","event_uuid":"82ae4eca-cb1d-41dd-a461-2b6dd6609fd7","position":{"commit_sha":"d7d471cb3f9bdf6f504e72b63548ba3ac5d2c500","position":"1795280621315866001-82ae4eca-cb1d-41dd-a461-2b6dd6609fd7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"After review: the root is passed as str (config.repo_root() returns a Path; gate_runs takes str); the ff4a test's record_gate_run stub now accepts the repo_root keyword, otherwise it would raise in the daemon. Scope note: the gate BODY's own stores (sidecar, journal) are resolved by the gate work itself, which already receives its ticket/root from the request; this fix covers the gate-run index writes that leaked. Related suites: 65 passed; no .rebar/gate_runs left in the worktree.","timestamp":1795278320527299001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Handoff to F3 (coordinator reassignment). State: claimed by this session; plan in the description passed review-plan; fix implemented and committed locally as 0e9bc81c359 in worktree .rebar/worktrees/f2-icefish (branch f2-icefish), NOT pushed to Gerrit. Its slot make verify was started and then stopped on the reassignment, so it has no verify result. Evidence: the deterministic reproduction and RED/GREEN regression test described in the ticket; related suites 65 passed. F3 may reuse the commit or redo it; the claim needs releasing or re-assigning before F3 claims.","timestamp":1795279764169608001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Re-reviewed after the file_impact change: PASS, certified at 7b773a77f5e. Advisory residuals recorded, not in this fix: (a) the gate body work() run on the daemon thread resolves its own roots for its own stores; the observed leak was the gate-run index only, which this fix pins. (b) config.repo_root() in _start_gate_job runs after begin_gate_job, as hold_owner_lock's internal resolution did before the change, so an exception there behaves as it did.","timestamp":1795280621315866001}],"created_at":1795277074350330001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"81c7ec1c-9031-4d16-82e4-b288f2c83a19","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"beef-0e12-6db9-491d"}],"description":"## Observation\nGerrit 3506 patch set 2 (3df64d38e14, a change that only edits tests/_isolation.py, the isolation-guard tests and a Windows deselect list) got Verified -1 from CI run 44911300869, job 136870796494 (`pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)`). 3 unrelated tests errored together with `Failed: New entries appeared in REPO_ROOT during this test: ['.rebar/gate_runs']` (test_completion_verifier::test_completion_verdict_pins_to_schema, test_observability_journal_bounding_1205::test_steady_state_run_does_not_read_a_whole_copy_of_the_journal, test_web_tool_gating::test_pass1_chunk_threads_web_from_criterion_routing). Some test on another xdist worker created `<checkout>/.rebar/gate_runs` in that window.\n\n## Root cause (verified)\n`_start_gate_job` / `_spawn_gate_daemon` in `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` start the gate on a daemon thread that outlives the request, and every gate-run write (`hold_owner_lock`, both `record_gate_run` calls, `release_owner_lock`) passed no `repo_root`, so `rebar.llm.gate_runs` resolved `config.repo_root()` at write time. The daemon's terminal record is written after the request returns; in the suite, the starting test (for example `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`, whose `store` fixture sets REBAR_ROOT through monkeypatch) can end first, its monkeypatch is undone, and the daemon then resolves the root from the worker's restored environment, the checkout, writing `<checkout>/.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>`. The leak guard of whichever tests are running on the other workers then fails them.\n\nDeterministic reproduction (Nov 21 2026): start a gate job with REBAR_ROOT=A, hold its work on an Event, change REBAR_ROOT to B, release. Before the fix: A holds the running record and the owner-lock file, B receives the terminal record. A regression test doing exactly this, `test_gate_daemon_writes_its_terminal_record_to_the_root_it_started_in`, fails without the fix (A's record stays `running`) and passes with it.\n\nThe same defect exists in production: an MCP server process whose REBAR_ROOT or cwd changes during a long gate would file the terminal record and release the lock in a different repository.\n\n## Approach\nResolve the root once, on the requesting thread, and pass it to every gate-run write for that job:\n- `_start_gate_job`: `root = config.repo_root()` before taking the owner lock; pass `repo_root=root` to `hold_owner_lock`, the running `record_gate_run`, and `_spawn_gate_daemon`.\n- `_spawn_gate_daemon`: new keyword `repo_root=None`, resolved on the calling thread when absent (direct callers in tests keep working); the daemon's terminal `record_gate_run` and `release_owner_lock` use it.\nNo config key, environment variable or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`\n\n## Testing\n- The regression test above: RED without the change, GREEN with it (both recorded here).\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`, `test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py`, `test_opcert_binding_thread_propagation_ff4a.py` and the async-transition tests pass (120 passed).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction of the leak is recorded here.\n- [ ] Every gate-run write of a job uses the root resolved when the job started, with a regression test that fails without the fix.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes and Gerrit gives Verified +1.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"resolve the gate-run root once at job start"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py","reason":"regression test for the terminal-record root"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_binding_thread_propagation_ff4a.py","reason":"record_gate_run stub accepts the repo_root keyword"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c113a443-ed48-4dff-9293-b8bc818dc31e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e6f5-f793-67a1-443b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP gate daemon resolves the store root at write time, so its terminal record can land in another repository (leaks .rebar/gate_runs into the checkout under test)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ed4bb4c3-36a1-4794-8516-a3fd3137ce54","81c7ec1c-9031-4d16-82e4-b288f2c83a19","8f69edbc-8f57-432a-a818-137a7b7b926e","8b60baa8-324d-4670-a4c7-724b691b6d61","c31058f7-071a-4972-a175-cc900f0f231d","c113a443-ed48-4dff-9293-b8bc818dc31e","68ade282-0219-48b2-ae2e-b1101a3906e2","1410b19f-a02b-447a-a700-09987e8746bc","6a104e5d-0c68-497c-b95c-f7ec49156dcf","c1943a27-b90e-4adb-9700-a0b0cf9b3dbd","f86d8a45-a5f1-4ceb-8154-0f0ae4f325f3","82ae4eca-cb1d-41dd-a461-2b6dd6609fd7"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795280621315866002,"uuid":"5649eb7d-1c1b-4c2a-b975-bbb15f77a446"}